# `hold-needed`: a function lifts over a sigiled argument at its type variable, even when
# its other arguments already made that variable an event; only a hold, `{!e}`, keeps the
# event whole there (Jimmy's ruling of 12 November: the braces are mandatory for
# functions and constructors alike).
Heard: fn [!Nat], !Nat -> [!Nat]
fn Heard events, !e = Push events, !e
